; NextDAAD SP18 item 7 Task 12 fixture - the two-channel sampled-effect
; API: auto-allocation, stealing, pinned channels and per-channel stops.
;
; Compiled by tests\build-tests.ps1 on every run (a break in the DSF is
; caught even without the leg switch, same rule the other fixtures
; follow); staged as the active GAME.DDB in sd\SFX2\ by
; tests\build-tests.ps1 -Sfx2, which also generates and stages the three
; stimulus WAVs described below as 001.WAV, 002.WAV and 003.WAV.
; sd\SFX2\ is emptied and refilled on every -Sfx2 run and holds nothing
; but those three files plus a NEXTDAAD.NEX copy of build\nextdaad.nex -
; copy the folder to the card and launch from inside it.
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHY THIS FIXTURE EXISTS
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; Task 11 wired sampled-effect channel 2 end to end but nothing in DAAD
; could trigger it. Task 12 lands the author-facing API on top:
;
;   SFX n 1 / SFX n 2    play effect n once / looped, on a channel the
;                        interpreter picks (AUTO-ALLOCATION)
;   SFX n 11 / SFX n 12  the same, PINNED to channel 1
;   SFX n 13 / SFX n 14  the same, PINNED to channel 2
;   SFX 0 15 / SFX 0 16  stop channel 1 / channel 2 and release its pin
;   SFX 0 5              stop BOTH sampled channels and the AY effect,
;                        and release both pins (the superset)
;
; Auto-allocation prefers a channel that already caches the requested
; effect, then an idle unpinned channel, then STEALS one: a one-shot
; before a loop, and between two of the same kind the one that started
; longer ago. A PINNED channel is never taken by auto-allocation, even
; when it is idle - the pin is a reservation. With both channels pinned
; an auto trigger is DROPPED (a DEBUG build prints "SFX BUSY?" at row
; 30, column 50).
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE THREE EFFECTS
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; Effect 1 (001.WAV) - 16000 bytes of payload, 440 Hz, 16000 Hz mono
; 8-bit unsigned. Under SFX_WIN_BYTES (24576, src\nextdaad.inc), so it
; takes the COMPLETE arm: the whole file is resident in the channel's
; window and nothing streams.
;
; Effect 2 (002.WAV) - 12000 bytes of payload, 880 Hz (an octave up, so
; the two are audibly distinguishable when they play together), same
; rate and format. Also COMPLETE.
;
; Effect 3 (003.WAV) - 40000 bytes of payload, 220 Hz (an octave down).
; OVER SFX_WIN_BYTES, so it takes the STREAMING arm. It exists to be the
; THIRD, unseen effect the steal and pin-reject verbs trigger - a number
; neither channel caches, which is what forces the allocator past its
; two cheap cases and into the steal/drop decision.
;
; All three are generated inline in tests\build-tests.ps1's -Sfx2
; staging block by the same deterministic whole-cycle sine writer the
; -SfxLong leg uses (New-SfxLongWav): 8-bit unsigned, centred on 128 =
; DAC_SILENCE, whole cycles only so a loop seam does not click.
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE VERBS
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
;   PLAY1 / LOOP1   SFX 1 1  / SFX 1 2    effect 1, auto-allocated
;   PLAY2 / LOOP2   SFX 2 1  / SFX 2 2    effect 2, auto-allocated
;   DUO             SFX 1 2 + SFX 2 2     both effects at once, auto -
;                                         the headline claim, and what
;                                         boot autoplay triggers
;   PIN1  / PIN1L   SFX 1 11 / SFX 1 12   effect 1 PINNED to channel 1
;   PIN2  / PIN2L   SFX 2 13 / SFX 2 14   effect 2 PINNED to channel 2
;   STOP1 / STOP2   SFX 0 15 / SFX 0 16   stop that channel, unpin it
;   STOP            SFX 0 5               stop everything, unpin both
;   STEAL           SFX 1 2, SFX 2 1, SFX 3 1
;                   loop on auto (channel 1), one-shot on auto (channel
;                   2), then a third, uncached effect. Neither channel
;                   is idle and neither is pinned, so the allocator
;                   steals - and it must take the ONE-SHOT (channel 2),
;                   never the loop. PASS: the 440 Hz loop keeps running,
;                   the 880 Hz one-shot is replaced by effect 3.
;   BOTH            SFX 1 12, SFX 2 14, SFX 3 1
;                   pin both channels, then trigger a third effect on
;                   auto. Both channels are pinned, so there is nowhere
;                   to put it: the trigger is DROPPED. PASS: nothing
;                   changes audibly and a DEBUG build prints "SFX BUSY?".
;                   Type STOP afterwards to release both pins.
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; THE DDB BYTE-ASSERT (the fixture-stimulus rule)
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; DRC silently rewrites some condacts (BEEP tone range, PAUSE duration
; scaling - see tests\audlad.dsf and tests\sfxdi.dsf's own headers), so
; what the interpreter actually receives is verified against the
; compiled bytes, not assumed from this source. tests\build-tests.ps1
; dumps tests\out\sfx2.ddb and asserts that every SFX condact below
; (opcode 18 = $12) is present with its authored sub-command byte,
; INCLUDING the six new ones 11-16 - a DRC that clamped or remapped an
; unknown sub-command would otherwise ship a fixture that tests nothing.
;
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; CSPECT EXPECTATION
; ------------------------------------------------------------------
; Effects 1 and 2 are both under 24K, so both take the COMPLETE arm and
; BOTH CHANNELS PLAY CONCURRENTLY UNDER CSPECT - no raw SD is involved
; on that path. DUO (and boot autoplay) is therefore audible there as
; two overlapping tones, and every steal/pin/stop verb is observable by
; ear plus the DEBUG markers.
;
; Effect 3 is the exception, and expected: it stages its first
; SFX_WIN_BYTES through ordinary esxDOS reads and then the refiller's
; raw-SPI CMD18 polls find nothing behind CSpect's SD emulation and
; fail. Bounded by SFX_FAIL_LIMIT, so the channel stops cleanly rather
; than hanging. The STEAL verb's verdict is unaffected - what it proves
; is WHICH channel was taken, and that is decided before a single card
; block is read.
;
; On ZEsarUX the same effect 3 is refused earlier still, at the filemap:
; a DEBUG build prints "SFX FRAG?" (row 30, column 60) and falls back to
; the AY effect. That marker is itself useful - it says the allocator
; RETURNED a channel rather than dropping the trigger, which is exactly
; what distinguishes a steal from a rejection.
;
; Audio fidelity verdicts belong on silicon, not here.

; System flags used by name (DAAD BLANK template spellings)
#define fPlayer             38
#define fDarkF              28

/CTL
_
/VOC
NORTH  2  noun
SOUTH  3  noun
LOOK   4  verb
PLAY1  60 verb
LOOP1  61 verb
PLAY2  62 verb
LOOP2  63 verb
DUO    64 verb
PIN1   65 verb
PIN1L  66 verb
PIN2   67 verb
PIN2L  68 verb
STOP1  69 verb
STOP2  70 verb
STOP   71 verb
STEAL  72 verb
BOTH   73 verb
/STX
/0  "It's too dark to see anything."
/1  "I can also see:"
/2  "What now?"
/3  "What next?"
/4  "What should I do now?"
/5  "What should I do next?"
/6  "I didn't understand."
/7  "I can't go in that direction."
/8  "I can't do that."
/9  "I have with me:"
/10 "I am wearing:"
/11 " "
/12 "Are you sure?"
/13 "Another go?"
/14 " "
/15 "OK."
/16 "Press any key."
/17 " "
/18 " "
/19 " "
/20 " "
/21 " "
/22 " "
/23 "I'm not wearing one of those."
/24 "I can't. My hands are full."
/25 "I already have the _."
/26 "There isn't one of those here."
/27 "I can't carry any more things."
/28 "I don't have one of those."
/29 "I'm already wearing the _."
/30 "Y"
/31 "N"
/32 "More..."
/33 ">"
/34 " "
/35 " "
/36 "I now have the _."
/37 "I'm now wearing the _."
/38 "I've removed the _."
/39 "I've dropped the _."
/40 "I can't wear the _."
/41 "I can't remove the _."
/42 "I can't remove the _. My hands are full."
/43 "The _ weighs too much for me."
/44 "The _ is in the"
/45 "The _ isn't in the"
/46 ", "
/47 " and "
/48 ".#n"
/49 "I don't have the _."
/50 "I'm not wearing the _."
/51 "."
/52 "There isn't one of those in the"
/53 "Nothing."
/54 " "
/55 " "
/56 " "
/57 "I/O Error"
/58 " "
/59 "File name error."
/60 "Type in name of file."
/MTX
/0 "NEXTDAAD TWO-CHANNEL SFX FIXTURE (SP18 ITEM 7 TASK 12)#n"
/OTX
/0 "a brass lamp"
/LTX
/0 ""
/1 "The listening room."
/CON
/0
NORTH 1
/1
SOUTH 0
/OBJ
/0    1   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   _ _
/PRO 0
> _ _   AT 0
        PROCESS 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        CLEAR fDarkF
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        DESC @fPlayer
> _ _   PROCESS 1
/PRO 1
> _ _   PARSE 0
        REDO
> _ _   PROCESS 5
        ISDONE
        REDO
> _ _   MOVE fPlayer
        CLS
        RESTART
> _ _   SYSMESS 8
        REDO
/PRO 5
; ---- auto-allocated: the interpreter picks the channel ----
> PLAY1 _ MES "effect 1 once, auto - SFX 1 1#n"
          SFX 1 1
          DONE
> LOOP1 _ MES "effect 1 looped, auto - SFX 1 2#n"
          SFX 1 2
          DONE
> PLAY2 _ MES "effect 2 once, auto - SFX 2 1#n"
          SFX 2 1
          DONE
> LOOP2 _ MES "effect 2 looped, auto - SFX 2 2#n"
          SFX 2 2
          DONE
> DUO   _ MES "both effects at once, auto - SFX 1 2 + SFX 2 2#n"
          SFX 1 2
          SFX 2 2
          DONE
; ---- pinned to a named channel ----
> PIN1  _ MES "effect 1 once on channel 1 - SFX 1 11#n"
          SFX 1 11
          DONE
> PIN1L _ MES "effect 1 looped on channel 1 - SFX 1 12#n"
          SFX 1 12
          DONE
> PIN2  _ MES "effect 2 once on channel 2 - SFX 2 13#n"
          SFX 2 13
          DONE
> PIN2L _ MES "effect 2 looped on channel 2 - SFX 2 14#n"
          SFX 2 14
          DONE
; ---- per-channel and global stops ----
> STOP1 _ MES "channel 1 stopped and unpinned - SFX 0 15#n"
          SFX 0 15
          DONE
> STOP2 _ MES "channel 2 stopped and unpinned - SFX 0 16#n"
          SFX 0 16
          DONE
> STOP  _ MES "everything stopped, both pins released - SFX 0 5#n"
          SFX 0 5
          DONE
; ---- the steal case: the one-shot loses, the loop survives ----
> STEAL _ MES "loop on auto, one-shot on auto, then a third effect#n"
          MES "PASS: 440 Hz loop survives, 880 Hz one-shot is taken#n"
          SFX 1 2
          SFX 2 1
          SFX 3 1
          DONE
; ---- the pin-reject case: both channels reserved, trigger dropped ----
> BOTH  _ MES "both channels pinned, then a third effect on auto#n"
          MES "PASS: nothing changes, DEBUG prints SFX BUSY?#n"
          SFX 1 12
          SFX 2 14
          SFX 3 1
          DONE
/PRO 6
> _ _   WINDOW 1
        WINAT 0 0
        WINSIZE 25 127
        PAPER 0
        INK 7
        CLS
        MESSAGE 0
> _ _   MES "001.WAV effect 1, 440 Hz, COMPLETE#n"
        MES "002.WAV effect 2, 880 Hz, COMPLETE#n"
        MES "003.WAV effect 3, 220 Hz, STREAMING#n#n"
        MES "PLAY1 LOOP1 PLAY2 LOOP2    auto-allocated#n"
        MES "DUO                        both at once#n"
        MES "PIN1 PIN1L PIN2 PIN2L      pinned to a channel#n"
        MES "STOP1 STOP2 STOP           stop one / stop all#n"
        MES "STEAL                      one-shot loses to the loop#n"
        MES "BOTH                       both pinned, trigger dropped#n#n"
        MES "Boot autoplay starts DUO automatically.#n"
; Boot autoplay - two concurrent looping effects with no typing at all,
; which is the whole point of the task. STOP clears them.
> _ _   SFX 1 2
        SFX 2 2
        GOTO 1
/END
